The CosmetriScan project establishes a robust foundation for analyzing chemical usage patterns, formulation risks, and product diversity within the cosmetics industry. To extend its value, applicability, and analytical depth, the following future developments are proposed:
________________________________________
1.	Integration of Toxicological and Regulatory Databases
Incorporating external datasets such as EWG Skin Deep, EU cosmetic ingredient bans, and FDA advisories will enhance the safety profiling of chemicals, offering users a deeper understanding of health risks and regulatory compliance.
2.	Real-Time Product Label Scanning via Mobile App
Developing a companion mobile app with OCR capabilities can allow users to scan cosmetic product labels in real-time and receive immediate risk assessments based on the existing chemical analysis framework.
3.	Consumer Sentiment and Review Analysis
Integrating data from product reviews and user ratings across e-commerce platforms can provide insight into consumer perception, complaints, or experiences related to specific ingredients or brands.
4.	Category Expansion to Include Household and Personal Care Products
Extending the dataset and analysis to other product categories such as shampoos, detergents, and skincare can enable a holistic view of chemical exposure in everyday life.
5.	Brand Transparency and Sustainability Index
Creating an index that scores brands based on their ingredient transparency, use of eco-friendly chemicals, and safety compliance can help consumers make more informed, ethical choices.
6.	Machine Learning for Ingredient Risk Prediction
Applying machine learning models to predict the potential risk level of newly introduced chemicals or uncommon ingredient combinations can support proactive safety evaluations and clean product innovation.
7.	Interactive Ingredient Impact Visualizations
Future versions of the dashboard can include dynamic charts linking ingredient frequency with skin types, age groups, or regional usage trends to support personalized product recommendations.
8.	Open-Source Collaboration and Ingredient Reporting Tool
Establishing a platform where researchers, dermatologists, and consumers can report emerging concerns, submit new findings, and collaborate on ingredient safety will encourage shared responsibility and innovation in cosmetic science.
________________________________________
With these enhancements, CosmetriScan can evolve into a comprehensive decision-support tool for regulators, brands, dermatologists, and conscious consumers, fostering transparency, safety, and sustainability in the cosmetic industry.
 
